      "domain": "irrigation_planning",
      "title": "irrigation planning method",
      "summary": "An irrigation circulation plan handled channels with lower and upper flow bounds. It first fixed every lower flow and replaced each residual channel capacity by u-l, accumulating the induced net imbalance at every node. It added a super-source and super-sink with demand-balancing arcs (and a sink-to-source arc for an s-t instance), ran max flow, and declared feasibility exactly when every arc leaving the super-source was saturated; it then restored the lower flows.",
